  "caption_final": "Weekend box office, Friday 13 to Sunday 15 November: Ramayana: Rise of a Legend made ₹196 crore India net across all languages, trade tracker Sacnilk estimates. That is more than it made over its first Friday-to-Sunday weekend.\n\nThat first weekend ended on Diwali, Sunday 8 November, when the film made ₹56.15 crore. The holiday Monday after brought ₹107.50 crore, still its biggest day.\n\nSuriya's Scene, in Tamil and Telugu, was a distant second.\n\nTrackers count differently: Bollywood Hungama put Ramayana's second Saturday at ₹68.71 crore, Sacnilk at ₹72.90 crore and Koimoi at ₹76.15 crore.\n\nWhich film did you watch in a cinema this weekend?\n\nSources: Sacnilk, India.com, The Week, DNA India, Bollywood Hungama, Koimoi\n\n#Ramayana #Scene #BoxOffice #IndianCinema #idlynerd\n\nImage: World Of Ramayana (official trailer)",
